        <article><![CDATA[<ul><li>Every imported Doppel alert for a selected product becomes an <strong>observable</strong>, marked as Doppel owned.</li><li>Alerts that match your indicator rules also become <strong>indicators</strong>, with the alert ID, brand, states and a link to Doppel stored as metadata.</li><li>When Doppel archives an alert or marks it unrelated, its indicator is <strong>revoked</strong>. When the threat is taken down or the site is down, the indicator is <strong>deactivated</strong>. Records are never deleted.</li><li><strong>Threat Lookup</strong> checks Doppel live. Queue states you selected under Threat Lookup give <strong>Malicious</strong>; other open alerts give <strong>Suspicious</strong>; archived, unrelated or unknown values give <strong>Unknown</strong>.</li><li>On an observable, <strong>Open in Doppel Vision</strong> opens the alert in Doppel, and <strong>Doppel Submit</strong> reports a value Doppel doesn&#39;t know yet.</li></ul>]]></article>
